{
 "id": "02001521f786",
 "task": "When should we schedule maintenance on the charging stations in the Bolzano area to minimise impact on users? Propose concrete weekday/time windows backed by observed usage.",
 "preset": "maintenance",
 "engine": "claude",
 "model": "sonnet",
 "status": "ok",
 "started_at": "2026-11-14T06:45:21.636727+00:00",
 "markdown": "## Answer\nThe quietest observed window area-wide is early morning on Tue, Thu and Fri, 05:00-07:00, with Thu 05:00-07:00 at 0.066 occupancy [E2]. Area-wide occupancy over the window is 0.435, so these windows are well below average [E2]. The evidence is thin, with only 4-5 comparable dates per window [E2].\n\n## Key findings\n- Thu 05:00-07:00 has the lowest occupancy at 0.066 (5 comparable dates), followed by Tue 05:00-07:00 at 0.124 (4 dates) and Fri 05:00-07:00 at 0.146 (4 dates) [E2].\n- The quiet window closes at about 07:00. Weekday occupancy at 08:00 reaches 0.497 on Mon and 0.661 on Thu [E2].\n- Avoid Wed 20:00-22:00 at 0.72 (6 dates), Sat 21:00-23:00 at 0.654 (5 dates) and Mon 20:00-22:00 at 0.651 (4 dates) [E2].\n- The busiest site, BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, has occupancy 0.669, full_time 0.462, 203 observed starts and a peak at local hour 8 [E3].\n- BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 is quiet at different times from the area: Sat 19:00-21:00 at 0.449, Mon 15:00-17:00 at 0.465 and Fri 13:00-15:00 at 0.469 (4 dates each). Its busiest windows are Sat 12:00-14:00 at 0.875 and Fri 18:00-20:00 at 0.867 [E4].\n- BZ_BOEHLER_01 has one point and full_time 0.57, equal to its occupancy of 0.57, so its only point is busy that share of the time [E3].\n- Late-night cells show 0.0 or null in many places, and Saturday night is inconsistent (0.691 at 00:00, 0.821 at 02:00), so they are not a reliable basis [E2].\n\n## Recommendation\nSchedule routine maintenance on Tue, Thu or Fri between 05:00 and 07:00 local time, preferring Thu, and finish by 07:00 [E2]. For BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, use its off-peak windows (Mon 15:00-17:00 or Fri 13:00-15:00) only if work cannot be done early, and only as a provisional choice [E4]. Do not schedule work in the evening peaks on Wed, Sat or Mon [E2]. Where possible, take points out one at a time at multi-point sites to keep some capacity available.\n\n## Limitations & unknowns\n- Each quoted window rests on 4-6 comparable dates, and 44 cells in the area grid and 65 in the BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 grid are below the minimum of comparable dates [E2, E4].\n- Coverage is low for top sites: BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 0.147, BZ_P_VITTORIA 0.082, BZ_BOEHLER_01 0.227, BZ_C_AUGUSTA_01 0.044 and BZ_RESSEL_01 0.033 [E3].\n- 22 sites were excluded for under 24 h of exposure, and 43 of 51 sites have data in the window [E3, E1].\n- BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 has null data for most early-morning hours, so its quiet windows are weakly supported [E4].\n- The area is a bounding box, not the municipal boundary [E1].\n- The figures are occupancy observations, not energy, sessions, demand or faults [E1]. Data quality (stale flags, gaps) was not checked.\n\n## Sources\n- [E1] dataset_overview — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E2] hourly_profile(scope=bolzano) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E3] rank_sites(metric=occupancy) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E4] hourly_profile(scope=Neogy-AMPECO:78226) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14",
